BASE <https://vocab.qworum.net/qrmm.ttl>

PREFIX qrmm: <#>
PREFIX qrmd: <https://vocab.qworum.net/qrmd.ttl#>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX vann: <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/>
PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>

<https://vocab.qworum.net/qrmm.ttl>
  vann:preferredNamespacePrefix 'qrmm';
  vann:preferredNamespaceUri 'https://vocab.qworum.net/qrmm.ttl#'^^qrmd:anyIRI ;
  rdfs:label 'QRMM Ontology'@en;
  rdfs:comment '''
    A general-purpose ontology.
  '''@en ;
  vann:example '''
    PREFIX foaf:   <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/>
    PREFIX qrmm:   <https://vocab.qworum.net/qrmm.ttl#>
    PREFIX qrmd:   <https://vocab.qworum.net/qrmd.ttl#>
    PREFIX :       <http://site.example/>

    [] qrmm:begin [].

    :jonka
      a foaf:Person ;
      foaf:name "Jon Ka".

    :jimdo
      a foaf:Person ;
      foaf:name "Jim Do".

    << :jimdo foaf:weblog "https://weblog.jimdo.me"^^qrmd:anyIRI >> :acc :jonka .

    :acc qrmm:prose 'according to :object, :subject'@en.

    [] qrmm:end [].
  '''^^qrmd:turtle.

qrmm:prose a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:label 'Prose'@en;
  rdfs:comment '''
    This property is used for translating RDF statements into human languages. RDF terms are first linked with their human-language translations through `qrmm:prose` statements, and then the actual translation process involves replacing each term in an RDF statement with its prose literal.

    By default, in a human translation the subject's translation is placed at the beginning of the produced statement, the predicates's translation is placed in the middle, and the object's translation is at the end. Any `:subject` and/or `:object` placeholder in a predicates's translation will override these default placements.

    RDF statements whose predicate is `qrmm:prose` are normally considered metadata and they are not meant to be translated.
  '''@en;
  rdfs:range rdfs:Literal ;
  skos:closeMatch rdfs:label .

qrmm:begin a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:label 'Beginning of an RDF file'@en;
  rdfs:comment '''
    This is a marker to be placed near the top of an RDF file (Turtle, TriG, N-triples, N-quads) to ensure a non-truncated transmission over networks. This property implies that there is a `qrmm:end` property placed at the end of the file. Note that RDF formats that are JSON-based or XML-based do not need to use this property.
  '''@en.

qrmm:end a rdf:Property ;
  rdfs:label 'End of an RDF file'@en;
  rdfs:comment '''
    This is a marker to be placed at the bottom of an RDF file (Turtle, TriG, N-triples, N-quads) to ensure a non-truncated transmission over networks. When an RDF file received over the network contains a `qrmm:start` property but not a `qrmm:end` property, then the file is considered incomplete/truncated.
  '''@en.
